  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": null,
    "grammar": "Plural only: the scissors are, these scissors, some scissors. There is no singular a scissor. Count with pairs: a pair of scissors, three pairs of scissors. The same rule applies to other things made of two parts: pants, glasses (for the eyes), tongs.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "The sc at the start is a single s sound, and the stress is on the first syllable, which has a short i. The double s in the middle and the final s are both z sounds: SIZ-erz."
